.ie \n(.g .ds Aq \(aq
.el .ds Aq '
.TH fujicli-image-recover 1  "recover "
.SH NAME
fujicli\-image\-recover \- Recover a retained rendered JPEG by its camera object handle
.SH SYNOPSIS
\fBfujicli image recover\fR [\fB\-\-force\fR] [\fB\-\-delete\-after\-save\fR] [\fB\-d\fR|\fB\-\-device\fR] [\fB\-v\fR|\fB\-\-verbose\fR]... [\fB\-h\fR|\fB\-\-help\fR] <\fB\-\-target\-serial\-sha256\fR> <\fIHANDLE\fR> <\fIOUTPUT\fR>
.SH DESCRIPTION
Recover a retained rendered JPEG by its camera object handle
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
\fB\-\-target\-serial\-sha256\fR \fI<TARGET_SERIAL_SHA256>\fR
SHA\-256 fingerprint of the exact physical camera serial number
.TP
\fB\-\-force\fR
Replace an existing regular output file
.TP
\fB\-\-delete\-after\-save\fR
Delete the camera object after a verified local file save
.TP
\fB\-d\fR, \fB\-\-device\fR \fI<DEVICE>\fR
Manually specify target device using USB <BUS>.<ADDRESS>
.TP
\fB\-v\fR, \fB\-\-verbose\fR
Log extra debugging information (multiple instances increase verbosity)
.TP
\fB\-h\fR, \fB\-\-help\fR
Print help
.TP
<\fIHANDLE\fR>
Camera object handle reported by a failed render
.TP
<\fIOUTPUT\fR>
Output file (use \*(Aq\-\*(Aq to write to stdout)
